{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","soma"],"title":"Dhammā","html":"<article id='thig1.17'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Therīgāthā 1.17 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Nuns 1.17 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Bhikkhunīs </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Chapter of the Ones </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dhammātherīgāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Dhammā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Dhammā </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Piṇḍapātaṁ caritvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I wandered for alms </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>“As I was going for alms, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>daṇḍamolubbha dubbalā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>though feeble, leaning on a staff. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>leaning on a stick, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vedhamānehi gattehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>My limbs wobbled </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>all my limbs trembled, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tattheva nipatiṁ chamā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and I fell to the ground right there. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>and there I fell on the ground. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Disvā ādīnavaṁ kāye, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Seeing the danger of the body, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>As I saw the danger in the body, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>atha cittaṁ vimucci me”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>my mind was freed. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>in that moment, my mind was liberated.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Dhammā therī …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>The Elder Dhammā </span></p></article>"}
